---
import DataShopLayout from '../../layouts/DataShopLayout.astro';
---
<DataShopLayout current="atlas" title="The Pied-à-Pierre Atlas | DATA" description="Trace the people, places, references, and cultural memory behind Dossier 001.">
  <section class="page-hero atlas-hero">
    <p class="overline">Context layer / Atlas 001</p>
    <h1>A shirt you can<br />keep opening.</h1>
    <p>The Pied-à-Pierre Atlas turns one satirical image into an explorable record of places, references, and contested memory.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="primary-action" href="/atlas/">Launch the atlas <span>↗</span></a>
      <a class="secondary-action" href="/shop/">View Dossier 001</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="atlas-preview">
    <div class="atlas-screen">
      <div class="atlas-map">
        <span class="pin pin-one">01</span><span class="pin pin-two">02</span><span class="pin pin-three">03</span>
      </div>
      <div class="atlas-card">
        <p class="overline">Evidence card</p>
        <h2>From image to place</h2>
        <p>Every node answers a practical question: What am I looking at? Where did it come from? Why did it matter? What changed in the remix?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="three-up">
    <article><span>01</span><h2>Orient</h2><p>Start with the visible joke, then identify the people, symbols, and language inside it.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h2>Trace</h2><p>Move through locations and source material without losing your place in the story.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h2>Carry</h2><p>Return to the textile as an artifact whose meaning expands after the first glance.</p></article>
  </section>
</DataShopLayout>
